<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
&nbsp;<br />
<strong>RE:</strong> {{{Case.Booking_PNR__c}}}<br />
 &nbsp;<br />
Thank you for getting in touch with Qantas Customer Care. I’m sorry to hear your property was lost in-flight.<br />
<br />
I can confirm that a report was made to Qantas regarding your missing {{{Case.Lost_Property_Name__c}}}. The item was reported as being left onboard {{{Case.Flight_Number_With_Code__c}}} on {{{Case.Email_Departure_Date_Time__c}}}.<br />
<br />
<strong>Personal items under your care and control</strong><br />
<br />
We do our best to make sure your journey with us is safe and always prioritise helping you look after your belongings on board and at our airports.<br />
<br />
It’s also essential for our customers to take responsibility for their personal items while travelling, which helps us provide the best service possible.<br />
&nbsp;<br />
Unfortunately,&nbsp;we’re&nbsp;unable to offer compensation for&nbsp;lost&nbsp;items that were in your care. If you need further information about our&nbsp;baggage policy,&nbsp;visit <a href="https://www.qantas.com/en-au/help/contact-us/baggage-services">Baggage services | Qantas AU</a> on our website<br />
<br />
<strong>We're here to help</strong><br />
<br />
This letter may be provided to your insurer&nbsp;in&nbsp;support&nbsp;of your&nbsp;lost property&nbsp;claim.&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;</body>
